msgstr "Characters: %d / %d"

msgid "whats_new.1_3_0.text_element"
msgstr "New: text labels on the canvas. \"Add text to the table\" is in the project menu and the Ctrl+K palette. Double-click a label to edit the text, its size and colour. Labels move, resize, rotate, change layer, undo and export like pictures."

msgid "whats_new.1_3_0.text_old_versions"
msgstr "Older versions of the app do not show text labels. They stay in the world folder (canvas_extras.json) and come back when you open the world in 1.3.0 or later."

msgid "whats_new.1_3_0.start_backdrop"
msgstr "The start screen background now keeps moving even when \"Reduce motion\" is on."

msgid "whats_new.1_3_0.side_handles"
msgstr "Pictures and text labels have handles in the middle of each side: they change only the width or the height. For a text label, the side handles change the width of the lines, so the text reflows and the letters keep their size. Holding Ctrl (Cmd on macOS) while dragging a corner resizes freely, without keeping the proportions."

msgid "decor.flip_h"
msgstr "Flip horizontally"

msgid "decor.flip_v"
msgstr "Flip vertically"

msgid "decor.history.flip"
msgstr "Flip picture"

msgid "whats_new.1_3_0.flip"
msgstr "Pictures can be flipped: right-click a picture and choose \"Flip horizontally\" or \"Flip vertically\". You can also drag a side handle or a corner (with Ctrl or Cmd) past the opposite edge: the picture keeps growing, now mirrored."

